[70.799381, "o", "=== CLEANUP SCRIPT FIX - May 5 ===\r\n\r\nPROBLEM:\r\n--------\r\nThe cleanup.sh script was either deleting nothing or deleting everything,\r\nincluding .dSYM bundles we needed to keep.\r\n\r\nROOT CAUSE:\r\n-----------\r\nFilenames with spaces (e.g., 'MyApp 2.1 (build 447).dSYM') were being\r\npiped to 'xargs rm -rf' without proper quoting. When xargs received\r\n'MyApp 2.1 (build 447).dSYM', it split it on whitespace into separate\r\narguments: 'MyApp', '2.1', '(build', '447).dSYM'\r\n\r\nThis caused:\r\n- Deletion failures (broken paths don't exist)\r\n- Wrong deletions (if partial paths matched other files)\r\n- Unpredictable behavior\r\n\r\nSOLUTION:\r\n---------\r\n1. Moved 'rm -rf' inside the while loop where variables are properly quoted\r\n"]
[70.799429, "o", "2. Added 'read -r' flag to prevent backslash interpretation\r\n3. Added debug output to show what's being deleted vs kept\r\n\r\nKEY CHANGES:\r\n------------\r\nOLD: done | xargs rm -rf\r\nNEW: rm -rf \"$dsym\" (inside the loop with proper quoting)\r\n\r\nTESTED:\r\n-------\r\n✓ Correctly deletes .dSYM bundles >7 days old without matching .ipa\r\n✓ Preserves .dSYM bundles that have matching .ipa files\r\n✓ Handles filenames with spaces, parentheses, brackets correctly\r\n\r\nBackup of original script saved at: /home/user/scripts/cleanup.sh.bak\r\n"]
[70.799541, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[70.799572, "o", "root@539a0ed5d60e:/home/user# "]
